{"chunk_id": "239e19b66077", "text": "Arjuna, still disguised as a Brahmana after winning Draupadi at her swayamvara, confronts Karna on the battlefield. Karna, sensing extraordinary skill, wonders if his opponent is a god or legendary warrior. Arjuna maintains the Brahmana disguise but declares he has mastered divine weapons and intends to defeat Karna. Respecting the supposed Brahmanical power, Karna withdraws. Elsewhere Bhima wrestles the mighty Salya and dramatically throws him down, astonishing the gathered kings, who begin to suspect the mysterious Brahmanas are no ordinary men. Krishna also perceives the truth\u2014that they are the sons of Kunti\u2014and persuades the monarchs to cease fighting. The Pandavas return to their humble dwelling and present Draupadi to their mother as \u201calms.\u201d Without seeing her, Kunti tells them to share what they have brought, inadvertently creating the dilemma that leads to Draupadi\u2019s unique marriage to the brothers.\nAfter the swayamvara fight ends, Kunti unknowingly tells her sons to share their \u2018alms,\u2019 creating the dilemma that Draupadi may become wife to all five Pandavas.\nThemes: mistaken command, dharma dilemma, identity concealment, aftermath of swayamvara, family authority", "vector": [0.005441888235509396, -0.01972137577831745, -0.005775065161287785, 0.005196212325245142, -0.010002035647630692, 0.03370807319879532, -0.02120216190814972, 0.0007206211448647082, -0.030234957113862038, -0.02808108739554882, 0.007336621172726154, 0.010008767247200012, -0.0030490728095173836, 0.018375206738710403, -0.004395241849124432, 0.013084763661026955, 0.03815042972564697, -0.019277140498161316, 0.014632857404649258, -0.028700323775410652, -7.624785939697176e-05, -0.011866480112075806, -0.0033687881659716368, 0.015319404192268848, -0.036400411278009415, 0.024581046774983406, 0.010183769278228283, -0.01680018939077854, 0.008790483698248863, -0.009295297786593437, -0.012721297331154346, 0.0009061400196515024, -0.